AGENTS.md tells agents to run 'pnpm run format' (prettier --write .).
Trunk scopes prettier away from **/*.ts, **/*.js and **/*.json - biome
owns those (single quotes, no semicolons) - and away from .agents/ and
.serena/, but nothing told prettier itself. Run as documented at
09a482c, the script rewrote 39 files (+4727/-4241) into prettier style,
after which 'biome check' failed with 37 errors: an agent obeying the
rule file broke the lint gate.

A .prettierignore mirroring trunk's scoping (plus the generated
lockfile) makes the documented command a safe no-op on a clean tree:
zero files differ, and biome stays green.
---
 .prettierignore | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .prettierignore

diff --git a/.prettierignore b/.prettierignore
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c0da961
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.prettierignore
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Mirror trunk's scoping (.trunk/trunk.yaml): biome formats TypeScript,
+# JavaScript and JSON (see biome.json), so prettier must leave them alone.
+**/*.ts
+**/*.js
+**/*.json
+
+# Agent context trunk excludes from every linter, and the generated lockfile.
+.agents/
+.serena/
+pnpm-lock.yaml
